Redistributed third-party software
----------------------------------

The releases of this repository tagged `refinery-v*` contain compiled binaries
of `refinery_cli`, from the refinery project:

    https://github.com/rust-db/refinery
    Copyright (c) 2018 Katharina Fey and the refinery contributors

refinery's crates are licensed `MIT OR Apache-2.0`. The upstream repository
distributes only the MIT licence text, so these binaries are redistributed
under the **MIT option** of that dual licence. A copy of upstream's LICENSE is
included inside every release archive.

These binaries are built from the unmodified crates.io source of `refinery_cli`
with the following build-level differences from a plain `cargo install`, all of
which are recorded in the `BUILDINFO.txt` inside each archive:

  1. On Linux only, a `[target.'cfg(target_os = "linux")'.dependencies]` entry
     is appended to `Cargo.toml` to build OpenSSL from source via `openssl-src`,
     so the resulting musl binary is fully static. This adds no code to refinery
     and changes no refinery behaviour.
  2. `LIBSQLITE3_FLAGS=-DSQLITE_ENABLE_MATH_FUNCTIONS` and
     `[profile.release] lto = true, codegen-units = 1` are set explicitly,
     replicating upstream's own build settings, which live in files that are not
     part of the published crate.
  3. `strip = "symbols"` is set to reduce download size.

Each release archive also contains a `THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md` listing the Rust
crates statically linked into the binary, and the C libraries it embeds:

  * SQLite  - public domain (bundled, compiled from source)
  * zlib    - zlib licence (via libz-sys, compiled from source)
  * OpenSSL - Apache-2.0 (Linux archives only; macOS and Windows use the
              operating system's TLS stack instead)

